# JSON Parameter Exchange

## Purpose

> **Scope:** Emit and consume machine-readable parameter documents in place of, or
> alongside, the question surfaces of the document and maintenance workflows.
> **Key items:** emission trigger, diagnostic output, emitted document, parameter
> catalog, returned document, authority

This file defines how {{skill-title}} exposes its pending questions as JSON and how it
consumes JSON answers.

## When To Emit

When the request asks for the questions, settings, or parameters "in JSON", "as
JSON", or another machine-readable format, emit a parameter document instead of
the question prompts.

Detection and default resolution still run first: the document contains only the
questions that are actually pending in this session.

Emit the document where the request directs - inline in the response by default,
inside a fenced `json` block.

## Diagnostic Output

When the request names a debugging mode, a diagnostic mode, a timing mode, or asks
for detailed or verbose information, emit the parameter document for information
purposes only.

The informational mode never triggers this emission - it arms only the elapsed-time
report in `process/operation-timing.md`.

The document covers only surfaces that are actually pending - diagnostics expose
the intake state and never create a question.

When no surface is pending, nothing emits - no parameter document, no
pending-decisions note, and no question prompts.

The emission order is fixed: the JSON document first, then a text description of
the pending decisions, then the question prompts.

The question prompts still run. The emitted document does not replace the
question flow.

## Emitted Document

The document carries a `description`, context fields (`target`, `task`, `date`,
`time`), and an `intake` array.

- `target` - the document or repository the task centers on.
- `task` - the classified operation: {{task-vocabulary}}, or empty for
  enable mode.
- `date` - the current day in `YYYY-MM-DD` format.
- `time` - the local time in `hh:mm:ss` followed by the timezone offset.

Each parameter object keeps a fixed key order: `id`, `question`, `answer`,
`description`, optional `when`, `type`, `menu`, `open`, `default` - the `default`
key is always the last key of the object.

- `id` - a stable kebab-case identifier for the parameter.
- `question` - the literal question wording presented to the answering side.
- `answer` - emitted as an empty string, or an empty array for `selection`, to be
  filled by the answering side.
- `description` - what the parameter controls and the detection evidence behind
  its default.
- `when` - an optional condition under which the parameter is asked, written as
  clauses such as `{{example-param}} is A` joined by `and` or `or` and grouped with
  parentheses. A parameter whose `when` is unsatisfied is skipped - it is not
  asked, applies no `default`, and ignores any returned answer. `when` may
  reference only parameters listed earlier in `intake`.
- `type` - `choice` for a single-option answer from `menu`, `selection` for
  multiple options, or `text` for free input.
- `menu` - required for `choice` and `selection`, omitted for `text`, letter-keyed
  (`A`, `B`, `C`, ...), with the recommended option labeled `(recommended)`. A
  menu lists at most three candidates plus a trailing
  `Cancel - abort the operation` entry, and `Cancel` is never the `default`.
- `open` - whether the answer is open to free text beyond the listed options.
- `default` - the option letter or suggested text applied when the answer stays
  empty - for `selection`, the array of letters that are pre-checked.

```json
{
    "description": "Intake parameters for <target>",
    "target": "<document-or-repo>",
    "task": "design",
    "date": "2026-10-30",
    "time": "09:14:03+02:00",
    "intake": [
        {
            "id": "document-type",
            "question": "Which document type should this produce?",
            "answer": "",
            "description": "Detected as requirements from the request wording.",
            "type": "choice",
            "menu": {
                "A": "requirements-document (recommended)",
                "B": "architecture-document",
                "C": "product-design-document",
                "D": "Cancel - abort the operation"
            },
            "open": false,
            "default": "A"
        }
    ]
}
```

